cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mrwin: Skeleton implementation for causal win statistics with instrumental variables"
version: "0.1.0-arxiv-theory"
type: software
message: "If you use this software or methodological skeleton, please cite the archived Zenodo release and the associated arXiv preprint."
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyen
    given-names: Thien Minh
    affiliation: "University of Medicine and Pharmacy at Ho Chi Minh City, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1090-6228"
abstract: "mrwin is a theory-first skeleton implementation for causal win statistics integrating instrumental variable estimation with hierarchical composite endpoints. The package provides pseudocode and early implementation scaffolding for the continuous Causal Win Ratio, Instrument-Standardized Gradient scaling, GLS pooling of adjacent genetic-instrument strata, multiplier bootstrap variance estimation with GWAS uncertainty propagation, and the Step-Down Pleiotropy Diagnostic. This release is intended to accompany a theory-only arXiv preprint and does not contain validated simulation results or empirical applications."
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - win ratio
  - Mendelian randomization
  - instrumental variables
  - hierarchical composite endpoints
  - multiplier bootstrap
  - biostatistics
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nguyenminh2301/mrwin"
date-released: "2026-05-26"
